class:: VisualEvent
summary:: Convenience factory for one-off visual events
categories:: Libraries>VisualServer
related:: Classes/VisualServer, Classes/Vbind, Guides/VisualServer

description::

A small helper that builds an link::Classes/Event:: with the right code::\type:: so it can be played directly (code::().play::) without a pattern. The event types it targets are defined in code::VisualEventTypes.scd:: and must be loaded first.

These are equivalent: code::VisualEvent.circle(0, 0, 50).play:: and code::(type: \visual, instrument: \circle, x: 0, y: 0, size: 50).play::.

CLASSMETHODS::

method:: new
Build an event of the given type.
argument:: type
Event type symbol (default code::\visual::).
argument:: args
An link::Classes/Event:: / association collection copied into the event.
returns:: the link::Classes/Event::.

method:: circle
A code::\visual:: event with code::instrument: \circle::.
argument:: x
argument:: y
argument:: size
argument:: color
code::nil:: -> code::Color.white::.
argument:: dur
argument:: view

method:: pulse
A code::\vpulse:: event.
argument:: x
argument:: y
argument:: startSize
argument:: endSize
argument:: color
argument:: dur
argument:: view

method:: line
A code::\vline:: event.
argument:: x1
argument:: y1
argument:: x2
argument:: y2
argument:: color
argument:: width
argument:: dur
argument:: view

method:: live
A code::\vlive:: event (code::dur:: defaults to code::inf::).
argument:: x
argument:: y
argument:: size
argument:: color
argument:: dur
argument:: view

EXAMPLES::

code::
VisualEvent.circle(0.3, -0.2, 70, Color.cyan, 1, \demo).play;
VisualEvent.pulse(0, 0, 10, 250, Color.red, 1.2, \demo).play;
::
